# crelyst — Next.js Guard Rails

## File and routing

- App Router only (`app/`). No `pages/` router.
- Do not delete route segments, `loading.tsx`, or admin auth shells without user confirmation.
- Public marketing routes and `app/admin/*` share patterns—preserve admin layout guards when adding admin pages.

## Data layer (internal API, not Express)

- Domain APIs live under `app/api/*` and delegate to `handleApiRoute` in `app/_server/lib/api/routeHandler.ts`.
- Controllers and Firestore access live under `app/_server/controllers/` and `app/_server/lib/firestore/`.
- **Server Components**: prefer `serverFetchJson` / `serverFetchJsonOrNull` from `app/_server/lib/api/serverFetch.ts` for reads.
- **Client Components**: use `callApi` from `lib/services/callApi.ts` with typed endpoints in `lib/constants/endpoints.ts` (`/api` base).
- Do not add a separate Express server inside this repo or call `crelyst-backend` unless the user explicitly wires integration.

## Auth and admin

- Admin auth uses Firebase + session cookies; preserve `protectRoutes` / access types on new admin API routes.
- Admin mutations under `/api/admin` may trigger audit logging via `recordAdminAuditLog`—do not disable unless asked.

## Components and styling

- UI under `components/` + `components/ui/` (shadcn). Tailwind v4 via `app/globals.css`.
- Zustand stores in `lib/` for client state where already used.

## Styling and SEO

- Extend Tailwind classes; avoid mass-replacing existing class strings.
- Use `metadata` / shared SEO helpers on server pages.

## Testing

- Vitest projects: `test:unit`, `test:integration`, `test:phase` in `package.json`—add tests in the same style as existing `*.test.ts` / `*.integration.test.ts` under `app/_server/`.

## Boundaries

- Never import server-only modules (`app/_server/*`, `firebase-admin`) into Client Components.
- Keep Zod validation aligned with existing API controller patterns.
